-- Costa Rica deep-dive content (English). Costa Rica's Comprobantes
-- Electrónicos regime, run by DGT (Dirección General de Tributación)
-- under the Ministerio de Hacienda, is a genuine clearance model: DGT
-- must accept a document before it's a valid tax voucher. It's also a
-- country in the middle of real technical transition -- schema v4.4
-- became mandatory 1 September 2025, the new TRIBU-CR platform replaced
-- ATV on 6 October 2025, and a further alphanumeric-cédula/schema-patch
-- cutover is expected 1 November 2026. Live-researched against
-- Hacienda's own site (hacienda.go.cr), the official DGT-R-012-2018
-- resolution text, Costa Rican press, and industry tax-technology
-- advisories (Voxel Group, EDICOM, FacturaSimple, Alegra). Penalty
-- article numbers (CNPT Arts. 85, 85 bis, 86) are corroborated across
-- multiple independent sources including a real 2024 enforcement report,
-- but could not be independently pulled from pgrweb.go.cr's live legal
-- text in this pass -- see the note on the penalties card below.









